Translate DNA sequences to amino acid sequences.

## Steps

1. Select `Sequences` in the navigation bar {% ref id="A" /%}.
2. Open `Translate sequences` from the tool list on wide windows, or select the tool name {% ref id="B" /%} at the top of the page to switch tools.
3. Add the input files {% ref id="C" /%} with `Browse files`, `Browse folder`, or `Open archive`. SEGUI searches a folder and its subfolders for files that match the tool's input format. See [file input](/docs/gui-usage/intro/#file-input) for mobile options.
4. Select `Browse` under `Select output directory` to choose the output folder. On phones and tablets, enter a `Directory name` instead; SEGUI saves it in the app's own folder.
5. Select the output sequence format. Turn on `Set interleaved format` to write interleaved output (optional).
6. Select the translation table. The default is the standard genetic code.
7. Select the reading frame. The default is the first reading frame. Turn on `Detect reading frame automatically` to let the app choose the frame for each file instead.
8. Select the run button {% ref id="D" /%}, labeled `Translate`, to start the task.

## Output

The app will generate a file containing the translated sequences. The default name is the input file.

## Supported translation Table

The app supports the following [translation tables](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Taxonomy/Utils/wprintgc.cgi):

| Table No | Genetic Code                                                                                 |
| -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1        | The Standard Code                                                                            |
| 2        | The Vertebrate Mitochondrial Code                                                            |
| 3        | The Yeast Mitochondrial Code                                                                 |
| 4        | The Mold, Protozoan, and Coelenterate Mitochondrial Code and the Mycoplasma/Spiroplasma Code |
| 5        | The Invertebrate Mitochondrial Code                                                          |
| 6        | The Ciliate, Dasycladacean and Hexamita Nuclear Code                                         |
| 9        | The Echinoderm and Flatworm Mitochondrial Code                                               |
| 10       | The Euplotid Nuclear Code                                                                    |
| 11       | The Bacterial, Archaeal and Plant Plastid Code                                               |
| 12       | The Alternative Yeast Nuclear Code                                                           |
| 13       | The Ascidian Mitochondrial Code                                                              |
| 14       | The Alternative Flatworm Mitochondrial Code                                                  |
| 16       | Chlorophycean Mitochondrial Code                                                             |
| 21       | Trematode Mitochondrial Code                                                                 |
| 22       | Scenedesmus obliquus Mitochondrial Code                                                      |
| 23       | Thraustochytrium Mitochondrial Code                                                          |
| 24       | Rhabdopleuridae Mitochondrial Code                                                           |
| 25       | Candidate Division SR1 and Gracilibacteria Code                                              |
| 26       | Pachysolen tannophilus Nuclear Code                                                          |
| 29       | Mesodinium Nuclear Code                                                                      |
| 30       | Peritrich Nuclear Code                                                                       |
| 33       | Cephalodiscidae Mitochondrial UAA-Tyr Code                                                   |
